ond to fires when  burning materials are off-gassing expose  us to carcinogens and lead to higher  rates of cancer what is a new revelation  is that our actual personal protective  equipment our bunker gear is actually  infused with carcinogens that we now  know we're re-exposing ourselves time  and time again so this is a new uh  threat that has emerged new reality uh  of how we're being exposed to these  carcinogens  you also say that the companies that  sell this gear with this chemical are  engaged in a public deception  what do you mean yeah we we would really  like to know  when these companies knew  that these carcinogens were exposing us  and what did they do about it  and i can tell you from our end we know  that they've com they've denied any  wrongdoing  so for your firefighter members this  must feel like a great betrayal to be  furnished this gear only to learn that  it's causing a potential cancer  in my opinion it's led to countless  deaths amongst firefighters at a young  age  and we are committed to taking this  fight on uh our members spoke loud and  clear at our convention we don't want to  be in bed with any chemical companies  and when it comes to you know these  chemical companies and what they've told  us  we're actively pursuing congressional  hearings to bring people before congress  to find out what they knew when they  knew it and what did they do about it  because our members deserve answers and  our families of our fallen deserve  answers  it was the case of a massachusetts  firefighter paul cotter that helped to  spur the research i was diagnosed with  prostate cancer  in  october of 2014.  i had  treatment  surgery early in 15 and uh  had to retire  from a job at any point when you were  serving as a fire lieutenant on the  force there did you have any kind of  warning that there was this potential  harm from the turnout gear the chemicals  used to coat it  no none at all  none at all  no one ever no one ever  thought about the gears  